# How to produce a correct KDP book (EPUB 3.2 baseline)

`rebook` (`rust_book`, `S:/rust/rebook`) builds "Rust перед сном" — a 14-chapter,
Ukrainian-language book sold on **Amazon KDP**.

> **Status (band 1 done):** `src/epub.rs` is now a **real EPUB 3.2 builder** — a true ZIP
> with the fixed skeleton (`mimetype` stored + first, `META-INF/container.xml`,
> `OEBPS/content.opf`, `OEBPS/nav.xhtml`, one XHTML page per chapter) driven by
> `book.json`. The old placeholder (`create_minimal_epub` raw splice + `H`/`O`
> markers) and the fake AZW3/KDP markers are removed; `convert`/`kdp` now return a
> clear "upload the EPUB to KDP" error instead of writing marker files.

---

## 1. Amazon KDP accepts EPUB directly — no AZW3 needed

The **simplest correct path** in 2026: upload a **valid EPUB 3.2** to KDP. KDP converts it
server-side to the Kindle formats (KFX) automatically.

- Do **not** hand-build AZW3/KFX/MOBI locally (deprecated, niche, easy to get wrong).
- Upload target = **EPUB 3.2** (with `META-INF/container.xml` + OPF + `nav.xhtml`).
- Amazon limits: each XHTML file **< 30 MB**; original cover must be ≥ 1000 px longest side
  (JPG/PNG); metadata in the OPF drives the KDP kindle-title prefill.

## 2. A valid EPUB 3.2 is a ZIP with a fixed skeleton

An EPUB file **must** be a ZIP archive in this exact layout (first entry = `mimetype`,
**stored uncompressed**, no BOM):

```
book.epub  (ZIP)
├── mimetype                     # application/epub+xml  (STORED, first entry, no BOM)
├── META-INF/
│   └── container.xml            # points to the OPF (full-path: e.g. OEBPS/content.opf)
└── OEBPS/
    ├── content.opf              # <package> with <manifest> + <spine> + <metadata>
    ├── nav.xhtml                # EPUB 3 navigation document (linked from the OPF)
    └── chapter-01.xhtml …       # real XHTML content pages (one per chapter)
```

Required, non-negotiable:

1. **ZIP container** — a real ZIP (crate `zip`), not a raw byte splice.
2. **`mimetype`** first entry, **compression STORED (0)**, exact string `application/epub+xml`,
   no leading BOM, no trailing form-feed.
3. **`META-INF/container.xml`**:
   ```xml
   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
   <container version="1.0" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:container">
     <rootfiles>
       <rootfile full-path="OEBPS/content.opf" media-type="application/oebps-package+xml"/>
     </rootfiles>
   </container>
   ```
4. **`OEBPS/content.opf`** — full OPF with `<manifest>` (list every file incl. nav + chapters +
   cover) and `<spine>` (reading order):
   ```xml
   <package xmlns="http://www.idpf.org/2007/opf" version="3.0" unique-identifier="book-id" xml:lang="uk">
     <metadata xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">
       <dc:identifier id="book-id">urn:uuid:…</dc:identifier>
       <dc:title>Rust перед сном</dc:title>
       <dc:creator>Artem Platinov</dc:creator>
       <dc:language>uk</dc:language>
       <meta property="dcterms:modified">2026-09-01T00:00:00Z</meta>
     </metadata>
     <manifest>
       <item id="nav"   href="nav.xhtml"          media-type="application/xhtml+xml" properties="nav"/>
       <item id="ch01"  href="chapter-01.xhtml"   media-type="application/xhtml+xml"/>
       …
     </manifest>
     <spine>
       <itemref idref="nav"/>
       <itemref idref="ch01"/>
       …
     </spine>
   </package>
   ```
5. **`nav.xhtml`** — EPUB 3 cross-reference: an HTML list with `<a href>` to each chapter
   (XHTML serialization, `<epub:type="toc">`).
6. **Chapter pages** — well-formed XHTML (UTF-8, `<html xmlns=…>`, `<head><meta charset/>` +
   `<title>`, content in `<body>`). Escape `< > &`. No bare ASCII in attributes.
7. **Cover** — optional OPF item `<meta name="cover" content="cover-image"/>` + image item;
   cover should be ≥ 1000 px.

## 3. How "Rust перед сном" maps into the skeleton

| Data in repo | Where it goes in the EPUB |
|---|---|
| `book.json` `title` / `author` / `language` | `content.opf` `<metadata>` |
| `book.json` `chapters[]` (14) | one `OEBPS/chapter-NN.xhtml` each + `<spine>` order + `<nav>` links |
| each chapter `poetic` | rendered inside that chapter XHTML (styled blockquote) |
| `cover_image` (optional `EpubConfig`) | `META-INF`/`OEBPS` image + OPF `<meta name="cover">` |

## 4. Rust implementation (done in band 1)

The builder in `src/epub.rs` follows this canon:

- `zip` crate (`zip = { version = "0.5", default-features = false, features = ["deflate"] }`).
  `mimetype` is written **first** with `FileOptions::default().compression_method(Stored)`,
  every other entry `Deflated`.
- `src/epub.rs` builds `META-INF/container.xml` (`full-path="OEBPS/content.opf"`),
  `OEBPS/content.opf` (metadata + manifest + spine for all chapters), `OEBPS/nav.xhtml`
  (toc links), and one `OEBPS/chapter-NN.xhtml` per chapter.
- Metadata (`title`, `creator`, `language`, `dcterms:modified`) comes from `book.json`
  via `rust_book::load_book` (`src/lib.rs::Book`). The `dc:identifier` is a deterministic
  v5-style UUID derived from title/author/language (`book_uuid`).
- Chapter content is XML-escaped (`esc`) then backtick spans are wrapped in `<code>`.
- `main.rs::build_epub` loads `book.json` → `generate_epub(config, &book)` → writes
  `build/rust_book.epub`.
- `convert_azw3` / `kdp_build` were placeholder-free stubs that wrote text markers; they
  now return a clear **"KDP accepts the EPUB directly — upload it"** error. There is no
  local AZW3 step.

